messages.reasoning_content:
`toComponent` doesn't exist on FRAME in this API version. Instead, use `figma.createComponent()` and move the child elements into it. Let's rewrite toComp: create a component, copy the layout properties, and move the child elements.

More simply: build the frame, then create a component, set the same properties, and appendChild the frame's child elements. Let's write a helper `frameToComp(f, name)`:

```js
function toComp(f,name){
  const c=figma.createComponent();
  c.name=name;
  // copy layout
  c.layoutMode=f.layoutMode; c.itemSpacing=f.itemSpacing;
  c.paddingTop=f.paddingTop; ... 
  c.primaryAxisSizingMode=f.primaryAxisSizingMode; c.counterAxisSizingMode=f.counterAxisSizingMode;
  c.counterAxisAlignItems=f.counterAxisAlignItems;
  c.fills=f.fills; c.cornerRadius=f.cornerRadius; c.strokes=f.strokes; c.strokeWeight=f.strokeWeight;
  const kids=f.children.slice();
  kids.forEach(k=>c.appendChild(k));
  if(f.width!==c.width) c.resize(f.width,f.height);
  f.remove();
  return c;
}
```

However, for fixed-size frames (arrows, 48x48), the sizing mode is FIXED. Copy those too. Also, for frames that have layoutMode NONE (arrows), copying layoutMode 'NONE' is fine.

Note: for auto frames, primaryAxisSizingMode is AUTO, so the component will hug. For fixed frames, the default is FIXED, and then resize afterwards.

Let's apply this fix and re-run.

